    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.cursorword\n\n### Description\n\nI get an error when moving the cursor over binary data especially null bytes (`^@`)\r\n\r\nI've tryed this:\r\n``` \r\n local status, res = pcall(vim.fn.match(curchar, '[[:keyword:]]'))  \r\n  if status then  \r\n    return res >= 0  \r\n  end  \r\n  return false  \r\n```\r\nbut the the error is still there?\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.7.2\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. `nvim -nu minimal.lua`\r\n2. require('mini.cursorword').setup({})\r\n3. create zip with uncompressed text data\r\n4. remove .zip extension\r\n5. open\r\n6. move around\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nerror free\n\n### Actual behavior\n\n```\r\nE5108: Error executing lua Vim:E976: using Blob as a String  \r\nstack traceback:  \r\n        [C]: in function 'match'  \r\n        ...nvim/pack/packer/start/mini.nvim/lua/mini/cursorword.lua:280: in function 'is_cursor_on_keyword'  \r\n        ...nvim/pack/packer/start/mini.nvim/lua/mini/cursorword.lua:138: in function 'auto_highlight'  \r\n        [string \":lua\"]:1: in main chunk  \r\n```",
