        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "You have just won \"The most unusual issue yet\" award! :joy:\r\nThe problem seems to be that cursor is positioned on multibyte character which is not fetched correctly. I'll think about a proper way to deal with this.\r\n\r\nMeanwhile, you can use a slightly modified version of your code (which threw error because call is executed *before* going into `pcall`):\r\n```lua\r\n  local ok, res = pcall(vim.fn.match, curchar, '[[:keyword:]]')\r\n  return ok and res >= 0\r\n```",
